  "question": {
    "text": "The maximum value of the function $f(x)=2 x^3-15 x^2+36 x-48$ on the set $A=\\left\\{x \\mid x^2+20 \\leq 9 x\\right\\}$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given, $\\quad A=\\left\\{x \\mid x^2+20 \\leq 9 x\\right\\}$ $=\\{x \\mid x \\in[4,5]\\}$\nNow, $f^{\\prime}(x)=6\\left(x^2-5 x+6\\right)$\nPut $\\quad f^{\\prime}(x)=0 \\Rightarrow x=2,3$\n$f(2)=-20, f(3)=-21$,\n$f(4)=-16, f(5)=7$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/mEW_vIq8xq9QBru_tFUMUU1wi-RfOrrWT0nYPgn4aLo.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nFrom graph, maximum of $f(x)$ on set $A$ is $f(5)=7$.",
    "image": null
  },
